#X obj 92 14 nn.act~ \$1;
#X text 200 10 [nn.neuron~] - one artificial neuron \, running at audio rate, f 76;
#X text 200 31 y = f( w1*x1 + w2*x2 + w3*x3 + w4*x4 + w5*x5 + b ). Five signal inputs x1..x5 are multiplied by their weights and summed (Pd adds signals that arrive at the same inlet) \, the bias b is added \, and the result goes through an activation function f (the curve in the box \, see [nn.act~])., f 76;
#X text 200 112 LEAK (optional): with "tau <ms>" the sum first passes a one-pole lowpass [lop~] - a leaky integrator. The neuron now has memory: this is the continuous-time recurrent neuron (CTRNN \, Beer 1995) that lesson 9 builds on., f 76;
#X text 200 178 ARGUMENTS: 1) activation name (default tanh) 2) net name: the neuron also obeys messages sent to [s nn-<net>] (default nn-0)., f 76;
#X text 200 214 MESSAGES: w <w1..w5> \, bias <b> \, act <name> \, tau <ms> \, randomize \, seed <n> \, spread <s> \, print. The face shows w1..w5 (green \, drawn range -2..+2) and the bias (purple). Drag them!, f 76;
